<h3 class="uppercase pixel-font">Shipping</h3>
<p class="text-large">Three weeks later, 400 books arrived at my studio. Cut, bound, and glued. A real book, a real product.</p>


<p class="text-large">In between, I'd made sticker packs and a small screen print to go with the pre-orders. I'd ordered hundreds of boxes, bubble wrap, envelopes, labels and tape.</p>
<p class="text-large">I numbered and signed all 100+ pre-orders from the campaign, along with the 120 screen prints I'd promised. The studio was a mess: cardboard and plastic everywhere, though it smelled pleasantly of fresh ink and paper. It took me a month to ship everything, carrying ten books at a time to the post office.</p>

<div class="video fade-in">
    <video autoplay loop muted playsinline src="/assets/img/book/NG_BooksEverywhere.mp4"></video>
</div>

<p class="text-large">They know me by name now. When I dropped off the copies for the book's contributors, the employee noticed Cory Doctorow's name.</p>
<p class="text-large">"Cory Doctorow?"<br>— "Yes," I said. "Have you heard of him?"<br>"I'm reading <a href="https://craphound.com/internetcon/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><em>The Internet Con</em></a> right now."</p>
<p class="text-large">Turns out I'm not alone in this open web-shaped rabbit hole.</p>

<p class="text-large">All orders have arrived safely with their owners. The feedback has been positive, and I love the photos people have shared on Nostr and Instagram.</p>
<p class="text-large">It feels like the project has concluded. Except…</p>

<h3 class="uppercase pixel-font">Selling a book</h3>
<p class="text-large">…250 books are <a href="/the-nogood-book/">still available</a>, out of a limited run of 400. I meant to print 300, but printing more is cheaper per copy, so I took a chance. A stack of boxes still lines the wall of my studio.</p>
<p class="text-large">For now, the book is only available on my website. I may offer it to a bookshop or two in Amsterdam down the line. This choice makes selling harder, but buying directly from the artist fits the spirit of self-publishing. It aligns with the control I want to keep over my work, and with the importance of building reach of your own through a personal website.</p>

<h3 class="uppercase pixel-font">Getting the word out</h3>
<p class="text-large">I asked my friend
    <a href="https://www.instagram.com/lilialand/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Lilia</a>,
    who shot the promo video while I was in the midst of producing the book, to do a photo shoot. We did it on the hottest day of the year so far: at 36°C the batteries overheated, and so did we. Challenging, but the results are wonderful. We celebrated with ice cream.</p>

