<p class="text-large">I spoke to <a href="https://primal.net/p/npub10xvczstpwsljy7gqd2cselvrh5e6mlerep09m8gff87avru0ryqsg2g437" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Eric</a> and <a href="https://primal.net/p/npub1equrmqway3qxw3dkssymusxkwgwrqypfgeqx0lx9pgjam7gnj4ysaqhkj6" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sync</a> on the <a href="https://fountain.fm/episode/WKPmEft6esngfKvtCJSi" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open Markets podcast</a> (my first!) about the origins of NoGood and the making of the book. I appeared on the <a href="https://fountain.fm/episode/ADC8esvhU6sK2R70VI4B" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Citadel Dispatch</a> as well. As a long-time listener to <a href="https://odell.xyz/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Matt Odell</a>, that was a great honour.</p>
<p class="text-large">If you have a podcast, I'd love to do more. I want to get better at talking about my work, and the reasoning behind it. Plus, I have this stack of books…</p>
<p class="text-large">Daniël <a href="https://www.daniel.pizza/journal/nogood-book/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">wrote a post</a> about writing the book, and about writing for someone who'd rather not talk about their work. Together we're assembling a press kit to send to websites and blogs covering independent publishing, graphic design and illustration, hoping it gets picked up here or there.</p>

